From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mathias Bynens <mathias@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 08:25:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [ui] Only open privileged URLs in new tabs when explicitly
 allowed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`UIHelpers.openInNewTab` blocked only `javascript:` URLs. Now it also
drops URLs without a web-safe scheme (such as `chrome:`, `devtools:`, or
`file:`) unless the caller passes `allowPrivileged`.

Opt in the internal uses that need this: the preloading infobar links
and the `<devtools-link>` context menu, which now respects the link’s
`allow-privileged` attribute.

Also, the DOM tree now renders `href` values of `<a>` elements as a
clickable `<devtools-link>` only for web-safe schemes. Other `href`s go
through the Linkifier, which renders privileged URLs as inert text.

Bug: 543907563
Change-Id: I1dd9a1256a9ed43698c550ad08773c8c84270456
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/devtools/devtools-frontend/+/8620439
Reviewed-by: Danil Somsikov <dsv@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Mathias Bynens <mathias@chromium.org>
(cherry picked from commit fb515cf1b180)

[FlyWeb] Clean pick onto the 156 gitlink 904b77f9fc; the DOMTreeElementWidget
change lands in ElementsTreeElement.ts (pre-rename name in 156). Upstream
reaches Chromium in roll 404327b549.
